# ---------- PrivGuard runtime data ----------
# Scanned/uploaded user files and scan output may contain real sensitive data.
# All mutable scan artifacts live under backend/var/ (uploads, extracted text,
# redacted copies, generated reports, scratch). One anchored rule covers them.
#
# NOTE: these rules are deliberately ANCHORED with a leading slash. Unanchored
# names such as "scans/" or "reports/" match at EVERY level, which would have
# silently ignored source directories like backend/apps/scans/.
/backend/var/
/uploads/
/scan_output/
/redacted/
/tmp/
/temp/

# Generated demo files in real credential and card formats (D-038). Fake, but
# secret scanners and GitHub's push protection cannot tell - so they are built
# locally by samples/make_secrets_finance_demo.py and never committed.
/samples/secrets-finance-demo/

# Local AI models and caches (large binaries)
/models/
*.gguf
*.bin
*.safetensors
.ollama/

# ---------- Local workaround (TEMPORARY) ----------
# Points npm's script runner at bash instead of cmd.exe, because the project
# path contains "&" which cmd.exe treats as a command separator. Hardcodes a
# Windows path, so it must NOT be committed - delete it once the project folder
# is renamed to a path without "&" or spaces.
/frontend/.npmrc

